Hook scripts for building
=========================

These hooks drive the build pipeline stages: init, pre-build, build, and
post-build. Each hook script defines the commands it handles via the
`<STAGE>_CMDS` variables and implements the corresponding `<stage>_hook()`
functions. See `example.sh.in` for details.

build-helper: Common helper functions

example.sh.in: Example of hook script

<priority>-<hook>.sh: Hook script for building

The `<priority>` numeric prefix (00-99) controls the execution order.
Hooks from the chip directory (`.chip/build-hooks/`) run before the common
ones. Run `./build.sh -h` to list the targets provided by the hooks.
